            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Anaerotruncus massiliensis,&quot; a new species identified from human stool from an obese patient after bariatric surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the main characteristics of a new bacterial species strain AT3(T) (CSUR = P2007, DSM = 100567) that was isolated from the stool sample collected from a 47-year-old obese French man after he underwent bariatric surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
